A||N||37||Boomtastic||What to do with those @#$% AOL discs?||||5||
Z||000000||Boomtastic||10-01-2001||07:33 PM||||For years we've all received them - shiny CDs filled with hours and hours of "FREE" service, but how many of these can you use in one lifetime? And what do you do with the CDs after you've used them up? That question has always haunted me, until now. This past weekend I was at a car show when I saw it - the ultimate use for an AOL CD! Here's the picture:<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSC00010_1.jpg">  <P>Yes, that's an AOL disc glued the front of an A/C compressor! Simple, shiny (although I would have glued it on backwards and lost the AOL label) and a legitimate use for an AOL disc! (Who uses them anyways?)<P>Have you seen/done better? Got pics? Let's see 'em ....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Boomtastic (edited 10-01-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||California Kid||10-01-2001||07:40 PM||||Hey.....Have ya ever put one of those CDs in the MicroWave Oven for 2 seconds??? Pretty cool result!<p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 10-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||10-01-2001||08:04 PM||||I have roll-up windows on the SE and when I carpeted the door panel I used a CD to put under the crank to keep it out of the carpet.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Gary||||reg||6
